        passageEn:
            "Kaung Htet wrote a set of instructions for the Nova School craft club so that everyone could fold their own paper boat.\n\nWhat you need: one rectangular sheet of paper.\n\nStep 1: Fold the paper in half lengthways, then unfold it to leave a crease down the middle.\nStep 2: Fold the top two corners down to meet the centre crease, forming a triangle shape.\nStep 3: Fold the bottom edges up on both sides to make a small rectangle beneath the triangle.\nStep 4: Carefully open out the shape and flatten it into a square.\nStep 5: Fold the bottom corners of the square up to the top point, then repeat on the other side.\nStep 6: Gently pull the two ends of the shape apart to open it into a boat.\n\nFinally, float your paper boat in a tub of water and watch it sail.",
        passageMy:
