        passageEn:
            "Zaw Zaw wanted to teach his little cousin how to make a paper boat, so he wrote out clear instructions first. \"Step 1: Take a square piece of paper,\" he wrote, remembering to number each step clearly.\n\n\"Step 2: Fold the paper in half to make a triangle,\" he continued, adding a small drawing to make it easier to follow. \"Step 3: Fold the two top corners down to meet at the center.\"\n\nHe kept going carefully. \"Step 4: Fold up the bottom edges on both sides. Step 5: Open the folded shape gently to form the boat's body.\" Each step used a clear command word, telling exactly what to do.\n\nWhen his cousin followed the instructions step by step, she made a perfect little paper boat on her very first try. \"Your instructions were so easy to follow!\" she said happily, floating her new boat in a bowl of water. Zaw Zaw smiled proudly, glad that his clear, numbered steps had helped her succeed.",
