        passageEn:
            "Before the end-of-year test, their teacher organized a review game combining everything the class had learned this year. \"I will read a sentence, and you tell me what grammar skill it uses,\" she explained to Moe Moe, Nay Chi, and Zaw Zaw.\n\n\"Nay Chi wanted to go, but it started raining,\" the teacher read first. \"That uses a joining word,\" Moe Moe answered quickly, remembering their Term 1 lessons about and, but, and because.\n\nNext came, \"She walked to the shop yesterday.\" Zaw Zaw raised his hand. \"That's past tense, because of 'walked' and 'yesterday,'\" he said confidently, recalling their Term 3 work on tenses.\n\nFinally, the teacher read, \"The elephant is bigger than the mouse.\" Nay Chi answered this one. \"That's a comparative adjective, 'bigger,' because it compares two things,\" she explained, pointing back to their pronoun and adjective lessons from Term 2. Their teacher smiled at their sharp memories. \"You all remember so much from this year. You're ready for anything on the test!\"",
