        passageEn:
            "For the final project of Term 1, Kaung Sett's class wrote an announcement poster for Nova School's Founders' Day fair. They began with a command to grab attention: 'Come and join the fun on Founders' Day!' Next came a question to spark curiosity: 'Have you ever tried the ring toss game?' Then the class wrote a statement listing the day's activities, carefully separated by commas: 'There will be games, food, and music.' They made sure to capitalise Nova School and Founders' Day throughout, since both were proper nouns. To keep the poster lively, Thidar added a compound sentence: 'The fair starts at nine o'clock, and it ends at four.' Finally, Kaung Sett finished with an exclamation to build excitement: 'What an exciting day it will be!' When the poster was complete, their teacher pinned it to the school notice board, and every single sentence type, comma, and capital letter the class had learned that term was proudly on display for the whole school to read.",
        passageMy:
